c, cmd-cb56f9a0108446f8, cmd-59ecee9bc26b4a79).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0075b5b6488e4b5c\",\"cmd-cb56f9a0108446f8\",\"cmd-59ecee9bc26b4a79\"]},{\"id\":\"req-5\",\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 stay separated from one another (VLAN isolation, not merely subnet mismatch)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node3 was given an address inside node2's own subnet (192.168.201.3) to rule out isolation being a subnet-numbering artifact; node2's ping to that address showed 100% loss with an INCOMPLETE ARP entry (cmd-71605834016a4d85, cmd-189052d39a26482c), proving true L2/VLAN separation. The same test was repeated after all three nodes rebooted with the same result (cmd-a181a5c41113460b, cmd-96bac714f5924c78), and the temporary address was removed afterward (cmd-2880f88612494b0a, cmd-4707a1e203854ad6).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-71605834016a4d85\",\"cmd-189052d39a26482c\",\"cmd-2880f88612494b0a\",\"cmd-a181a5c41113460b\",\"cmd-96bac714f5924c78\",\"cmd-4707a1e203854ad6\"]},{\"id\":\"req-6\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol: each managed node shows healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, and recovered VLAN/connectivity/isolation state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"For each of node1, node2, node3: a pre-reboot boot_id and healthy baseline was captured (cmd-29afaf6371cb4303/cmd-aad1a2d199f2401d/cmd-cfd3ba69ee774b4a, corroborated by fixed global:before_prepare boot-identity snapshots), a reboot was issued, a different post-reboot boot_id was confirmed (cmd-b00b70a8d1ba4d51, cmd-fcf334dfe0f44667, cmd-e8d94df5bda24ff4, corroborated by fixed global:after_executor boot-identity snapshots), and the VLAN bridge (auto-recreated by the systemd oneshot unit), static IPs (via systemd-networkd drop-ins), connectivity, and cross-segment isolation were all re-verified afterward (cmd-89ed88a578314933, cmd-b9241e5787dd4e9e, cmd-59ecee9bc26b4a79, cmd-96bac714f5924c78). node1's segmentation service ran itself to completion after boot without m